# config/packages.map — one package name, every family's spelling of it.
#
# Read by lib/pkg.sh (_pkg_map_load) and NOTHING else. Every module keeps ONE
# list of what it installs, written in the Debian names it always used; this file
# is the only place a family difference lives (spec 002 FR-007, plan D5).
#
#   debian-name   redhat   suse   arch
#
#   =         the same name as the Debian one
#   -         no package on this family: pkg_install logs "no <family> package
#             for <name>" and goes on — a skip, never a failure
#   a,b,c     several packages stand for the one Debian name (all are installed)
#
# THE DEBIAN FAMILY NEVER READS THIS FILE (FR-008). pkg.sh answers before opening
# it, so an apt box installs exactly the names the modules spell.
#
# A name with no row is looked up under its own spelling on every family. A row is
# still written for every name a default-set module uses, so "no row" never means
# "nobody checked". Names are matched the way each package manager resolves them
# on install — by what a package PROVIDES — so `=` also holds where a release
# ships the capability under another package name (Fedora's wget is wget2-wget,
# Leap's ffmpeg is ffmpeg-7).
#
# redhat is ONE column for EL (AlmaLinux, Rocky) and Fedora. pkg_ensure_addon
# (modules/00-preflight) enables CRB and EPEL on EL, so an EPEL name is simply the
# redhat name. A name only some releases of a family carry stays here as that
# name, and pkg_install drops it on the others with its usual "no installation
# candidate" warning; `-` is for a family that has no such package at all.
#
# Every row was checked on 2026-10-06 against the releases' own repositories —
# `dnf repoquery` on AlmaLinux 9/10, Rocky Linux 9/10 and Fedora 43/44 (EL with
# CRB + EPEL), `zypper search` on openSUSE Leap 16.0, `pacman -Si` on Arch. The
# trailing comment says where a name is NOT plain base-repository: "EPEL" means it
# comes from EPEL on EL; a release that lacks it is named.
#
# One row per line, whitespace-separated, `#` to end of line is a comment.

# --- 00-preflight: the bootstrap set ------------------------------------------
ca-certificates             =                         =                               =
curl                        =                         =                               =
git                         =                         =                               =
tar                         =                         =                               =
xz-utils                    xz                        xz                              xz
diffutils                   =                         =                               =
findutils                   =                         =                               =

